 ("h2", "10.1 Biomes of the World"),
 ("note", "DEFINITION", "A **biome** is a large natural region where certain types of plants and animals live under similar climatic conditions. (*bio* = life, from Greek *bios*.) A biome is a broad environmental region; an **ecosystem** is like a neighbourhood within it where living and non-living things interact closely."),
 ("p", "Biomes are decided by **temperature, precipitation, dominant plant species and growth forms of vegetation**. They are grouped as **terrestrial** (forest, grassland, desert, tundra) and **aquatic** (freshwater and marine). Major types on the world map: tropical rainforest, grassland, desert, temperate deciduous, taiga and tundra."),
