 ("h2", "10.4 Challenges and Government Support"),
 ("ul", ["**Challenges:** poor healthcare, education and clean water; fuelwood fumes harm women's health (**PM Ujjwala Yojana** helps); restrictions on forest use; floods, landslides and **forest fires**; crop damage and attacks by elephants, monkeys and wild boar; low prices for forest produce and lack of awareness of rights.", "**Forest Rights Act, 2006 (FRA):** recognises rights of eligible communities over forest land and resources, allows collection of minor forest produce and grants ownership of small cultivated patches.", "**Other support:** Joint Forest Management (JFM), PESA, DAJGUA, PM JANMAN, scholarships, health and skill programmes."]),
 ("note", "IMPORTANT", "**Mendha Lekha** (Gadchiroli, Maharashtra; Gond village) was the first village in India to gain rights over its forest under the FRA. Following **'Mawa Nate Mawa Raj' (our village, our rule)**, the Gram Sabha manages 1,800 hectares, regulates tree cutting, prevents fires, promotes bamboo harvesting and uses revenue for education and infrastructure."),
 ("h2", "10.5 Ecological Commons"),
 ("p", "**Ecological commons** are natural resources such as forests, rivers, lakes, grazing lands, air and biodiversity shared and used collectively by a community, often managed by traditional rules. Population growth, industry and privatisation are shrinking them."),
